---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../lib/data.js';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy" description={`${SITE_NAME} privacy policy.`}>
  <div class="neu box prose" style="max-width:760px;margin:40px auto">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>{SITE_NAME} does not ask for names, emails or any personal information. The list of codes you copied is stored only in your own browser (local storage) and never sent to us.</p>
    <p>If you play RoGuessr battles, we save a game profile: a random player name we generate (like "Turbo Panda 42"), your avatar, rating and game stats. It is linked to a random key stored in your browser. Nobody can type text or chat, and we never ask for real names.</p>
    <p>"Sign in with Google" is optional and only offered to players 13 or older (we ask the birth year, keep only a yes/no on your device and never send it to us). We store only a scrambled version of Google's account ID so you can find your profile again - not your email, name or photo. Younger players keep playing with the profile saved on their device.</p>
    <p>Our hosting provider (Cloudflare) may process basic technical data such as IP addresses to deliver and protect the site.</p>
    <p>The Real World game loads street photos from Panoramax servers and map tiles from OpenFreeMap. Like any image on the web, your browser connects to those servers to download them; we don't send them any account or game data.</p>
    <p>If we show ads in the future, they will be configured as child-directed and non-personalized, and this page will be updated.</p>
    <p>Never share your Roblox password with anyone. Real codes are always free - no website can give you free Robux.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
